<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Upper Valais</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valais">Valais</a> is the German-speaking eastern part of the canton of Valais in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, along the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> from the Rhône Glacier to around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leuk">Leuk</a>. Its communes, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zenden">Zenden</a>, gradually took power from the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Sion and ruled the French-speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-valais">Lower Valais</a> as a subject territory until 1798. Its main towns are Brig, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visp">Visp</a> and Naters.</p></div>
